# --- Server (local dev only — not used when deployed to Lambda) ---
PORT=4000

# --- MongoDB Atlas ---
# Team's cluster: M0 Free tier
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/wardrobe

# --- Auth: Phone OTP -> JWT ---
# PRODUCTION: JWT secret lives in AWS Secrets Manager, not here — set
# JWT_SECRET_ARN to the secret's ARN once it's created (services/secrets.ts
# fetches it at runtime and caches it across Lambda warm starts).
JWT_SECRET_ARN=arn:aws:secretsmanager:ap-south-1:720374066183:secret:wardrobe-jwt-secret-XXXXXX
# LOCAL DEV ONLY fallback — if JWT_SECRET_ARN isn't set, this is used
# instead, so you don't need real Secrets Manager access just to run
# `npm run dev`. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=30d

# --- Amazon S3 ---
AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
AWS_S3_BUCKET=superbae-media
AWS_BACKUP_BUCKET=superbae-media
# Local dev only — in Lambda, credentials come from the function's IAM
# role instead (see infra/serverless.yml), don't set these there.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-access-key-id
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret-access-key

# --- Amazon SNS (OTP SMS) ---
# Production access: currently PENDING — request it in the SNS console
# before real users can receive OTP texts. Until then (and for local
# dev), leave this false: the OTP code prints to the console instead.
SEND_REAL_SMS=false
# Rate limits enforced in code (services/otp.service.ts), not configurable
# via env — confirmed: 1 request per 60 seconds, max 5 per hour, per phone.

# --- Dev login (skips OTP completely — no SNS needed at all) ---
# Set to true only on your own machine for local testing. NEVER set this
# to true in any deployed/production environment — POST /auth/dev-login
# issues a real valid token for ANY phone number with zero verification
# when this is on. Leave commented out / false everywhere except local dev.
DEV_LOGIN_ENABLED=true

# --- Background removal (Add Items screen) ---
# Two providers:
#
#   removebg — remove.bg's REST API. Works for flat-lay/product photos
#     with NO person in frame. Does NOT strip a person out of the shot,
#     only the background behind them — a photo taken ON A MODEL still
#     shows the model after processing. Needs BG_REMOVAL_API_KEY
#     (remove.bg API key).
#
#   gemini — Gemini's image-editing model ("Nano Banana"). Genuinely
#     removes a person/model from the photo via a prompt, keeping just
#     the garment on a clean background. USE THIS if uploaded photos
#     are on-model rather than flat-lay. Needs BG_REMOVAL_API_KEY (a
#     real Gemini API key — same one used for AI_VISION_PROVIDER below
#     works fine here too) and optionally BG_REMOVAL_GEMINI_MODEL.
#
# Previously there was also a free 'garment_segmentation' option (a
# public Hugging Face Space) — removed. It was slow (15-45+s per
# image), had no uptime guarantee, and lower accuracy than a real
# production model. Gemini does the same on-model-photo job properly.
#
# CONFIRMED: on-model item photos, so set to gemini.
BG_REMOVAL_PROVIDER=gemini
BG_REMOVAL_API_KEY=
# gemini-2.5-flash-image ("Nano Banana") was the original pick here for
# cost, but Google has DEPRECATED it — official shutdown Oct 2, 2026.
# Migrated to gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image ("Nano Banana 2 Lite")
# instead of the full gemini-3.1-flash-image: confirmed via Google's
# own pricing page it's actually CHEAPER than the old 2.5 model
# ($0.0336/image vs $0.039) and ~2.7x faster, while the full 3.1 Flash
# Image costs roughly 1.7x more for 4K/Pro-tier quality this narrow
# task (isolate a garment, drop the person, transparent background)
# doesn't need. If Lite starts producing worse results than 2.5 did on
# tricky photos, gemini-3.1-flash-image is the one-line upgrade.
BG_REMOVAL_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image

# --- AI provider (Ara's outfit story + chat replies) ---
# CONFIRMED: GPT-5 mini via a DIRECT OpenAI API key (not OpenRouter —
# earlier drafts of this file pointed at OpenRouter's endpoint, but a
# directly-purchased OpenAI key only authenticates against OpenAI's own
# API, not OpenRouter's. Sending a direct key to OpenRouter's URL fails
# auth even though the model name looks similar — this is why chat was
# returning "Missing Authentication header" errors: OpenRouter was
# never getting a header it could recognize as one of its own keys, or
# fell back to a case where no header was sent depending on how it
# was misconfigured. Fixed by pointing straight at OpenAI here instead.
# Note the model name also drops the "openai/" prefix — that prefix is
# OpenRouter-specific routing syntax, OpenAI's own API doesn't use it.
# REQUIRED — without a real key here, EVERYTHING AI-related (chat
# replies, outfit stories, "how Ara thought about it") silently runs
# on the canned fallback text further down in aiStylist.service.ts
# instead. That fallback is deliberately serviceable, not a bug, but
# it's also why chat can feel repetitive/robotic if this is still blank.
AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
AI_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
AI_PROVIDER_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# --- Fallback AI provider ---
# If the primary provider above fails or times out, this second one is
# tried automatically before falling back to canned responses. Leave
# ALL THREE blank to run single-provider mode (primary -> canned text).
# CONFIRMED: Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite as secondary, so GPT-5 mini (primary)
# -> Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite (fallback) -> canned text. Gemini 2.5 Flash
# was an earlier default here but Google is shutting it down
# 2026-10-16 — 3.1 Flash-Lite is the closer-priced replacement ($0.25/M
# in, $1.50/M out vs 2.5 Flash's old $0.30/$2.50; Gemini 3.5 Flash also
# works but costs ~5x more on input for this app's usage pattern, which
# doesn't need the extra headroom).
# Fill in AI_FALLBACK_API_KEY with a real Gemini API key to activate this.
AI_FALLBACK_API_KEY=
AI_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
AI_FALLBACK_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- Vision provider for AI Color Analysis (selfie -> skin undertone) ---
# and the tag scanner (photo of a garment label -> brand/size/material).
# Needs a model that actually supports image input as well as text
# output — GPT-5 mini's vision support isn't confirmed, so this is kept
# as a separate config rather than assumed to work via AI_PROVIDER_*.
# CONFIRMED: Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite as primary vision provider.
# Fill in AI_VISION_PROVIDER_API_KEY with a real Gemini key to activate.
# Until a real key is set here, every color analysis returns the same
# "unknown" undertone + neutral-colors fallback — this is that fallback
# working as designed, not a bug, but it looks broken to a user because
# it can't say why it's guessing.
#
# IMPORTANT: a "Gemini API Key" name + a Google Cloud project number
# (e.g. "projects/790874505274") are NOT the API key itself — those are
# just identifiers. The actual key is a separate string that looks like
# "AIzaSy..." — grab it from Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com/app/apikey)
# or the Cloud Console's "APIs & Services > Credentials" page, then
# paste THAT string below, not the project number.
AI_VISION_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
AI_VISION_PROVIDER_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
AI_VISION_PROVIDER_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite

# --- Vision fallback ---
# If the vision primary above fails or times out, this tries GPT-5 mini
# before returning the static "unknown undertone" fallback. Same
# optional-chain pattern as AI_FALLBACK for chat: leave this blank to
# run vision in single-provider mode.
# CONFIRMED: GPT-5 mini as vision backup, via a DIRECT OpenAI key — same
# fix as AI_PROVIDER above (this app has a real OpenAI key, not an
# OpenRouter one, so this needs OpenAI's own endpoint, not OpenRouter's).
# Reuses the SAME key as AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY above — one OpenAI key
# covers both slots, no separate purchase needed. Its image-input
# support isn't independently confirmed the way GLM's wasn't either, so
# treat this as best-effort; if GPT-5 mini can't actually read images,
# this fallback will just fail silently and drop to the static
# fallback, same as any other misconfigured/incompatible provider would.
AI_VISION_FALLBACK_API_KEY=
AI_VISION_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
AI_VISION_FALLBACK_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# --- Monitoring ---
SENTRY_DSN=

# --- Bin retention ---
# 30 days, enforced by the binCleanup scheduled Lambda (infra/serverless.yml)
# — not configurable via env, hardcoded per the confirmed policy.
